# Force LF for files that run inside the Linux container — a CRLF shebang
# line ("#!/bin/sh\r") fails to resolve on Linux, breaking the entrypoint
# with a confusing "No such file or directory". Found when scripts/
# docker-entrypoint.sh picked up CRLF from a Windows edit and broke the
# Docker image on rebuild.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
# index.html carries an inline <script> allowed via a CSP sha256 hash
# (server/index.ts) — browsers normalize CRLF -> LF before hashing either
# way, so this doesn't change the hash, but keeping the source LF avoids the
# same confusion when recomputing it by hand after a future edit.
frontend/index.html text eol=lf
